    "title": "Report on Washington D.C. Shooting and Political Reactions",
    "text": "• A shooting occurred in Washington, D.C., near the White House on Wednesday afternoon.\n• Two West Virginia National Guard members were shot.\n• The Guard members were hospitalized in critical condition.\n• The suspect, Rahmanullah Lakamal, was also shot and sustained non-life-threatening wounds.\n• Lakamal is a 29-year-old Afghan national.\n• Lakamal entered the U.S. in 2021 through Operation Allies Welcome.\n• Vice President JD Vance stated the shooting validated his prior warnings about unvetted refugee resettlement.\n• Vance called for swift political action, including deporting individuals without the right to be in the country.\n• Former President Donald Trump posted on Truth Social, expressing support for the National Guard and law enforcement.",
